        "#**Phase 5**"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "This final phase aggregates the evaluation metrics across all trained architectures, providing a holistic quantitative overview of our generative modeling experiments.\n",
        "\n",
        "By observing the consolidated results, we can draw three major scientific conclusions from this project:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Architectural Depth Improves Fidelity (Phase 2):** Transitioning from a standard MLP baseline to a deep Convolutional network with Residual Blocks significantly minimized the reconstruction loss and allowed the model to capture high-frequency spatial features, ultimately leading to a State-of-the-Art FID score.\n",
        "2. **The Information Bottleneck Trade-off (Phase 3):** Through the $\\beta$-VAE experiments, we empirically validated the trade-off between visual sharpness and latent space structure. Higher $\\beta$ values heavily penalized the latent distribution, leading to *Posterior Collapse* but yielding highly disentangled, interpretable, and continuous generative manifolds.\n",
        "3. **Directed Generation via Conditioning (Phase 4):** By upgrading to a Conditional VAE (CVAE), we successfully offloaded the \"class identity\" from the latent variable $z$ to the explicit condition $y$. This resolved the issue of class ambiguity and enabled deterministic, highly accurate directed generation (achieving ~90% accuracy against a pre-trained classifier).\n",
        "\n",
        "Overall, this project successfully navigated the complexities of generative modeling, moving from a basic unlabelled bottleneck to a highly controllable and robust Conditional VAE."
      ],
